  "question": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ga</mi></math> (atomic mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>70</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></math>) crystallizes in a hexagonal close packed structure. The total number of voids in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>581</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ga</mi></math> is ________&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>21</mn></msup></math>. (Round off to the Nearest Integer).",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "15",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCP</mi></math> structure : Per atom, there will be one octahedral void <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>OV</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and two tetrahedral voids <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>TV</mi><mo>)</mo></math>.</p><p>Therefore, total three voids per atom are present in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCP</mi></math> structure.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>&nbsp;Therefore total no. of atoms of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ga</mi></math>&nbsp;will be-</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Mass</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Molar</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Mass</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>581</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>70</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>023</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>23</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> Now, total Number of voids <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo></math> total no. of atoms&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>581</mn></mrow><mn>70</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>023</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>23</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>99</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>21</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8771;</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>21</mn></msup></math></p>",
